course: dictionary
lesson: 13217
title: Fusty: a smell and an idea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a smell, and some describe ideas. «Fusty» does both. A room that has been shut up for a long time can smell stale and damp, and we call it fusty. Try the swap check: does «The attic was fusty» make sense if you think of a dusty, damp, shut-up smell? Yes, it does.
explain: The second meaning is about ideas, not air. «Fusty old rules» means rules that are old-fashioned and dull, as if nobody has looked at them for years. Look for clues such as old, shut, stale and long ago, and the words around them.
explain: Clues in a story help too. «The cellar was dark and fusty, and nobody had opened its door for years.» Dark, shut and nobody opening the door are the clues: the cellar is stale, damp and old. Mole's little home, shut up all winter, might be fusty when he comes back in spring.
fact: «Fusty» is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a fusty room, a fusty smell, fusty ideas.
fact: «Fusty» means smelling stale, damp and old, like a room shut up for a long time.
fact: «Fusty» can also mean old-fashioned and dull in ideas, as in «fusty old rules».
fact: Close words: musty is a close word for the smell sense, and «fusty» has the forms fustier and fustiest.
fact: When you meet a new word, ask what it describes: a smell, a place, or an idea. That tells you which meaning to try.
exercise: «The old trunk in the attic smelled fusty.» What does fusty mean here? | *Stale, damp and old | Loud and noisy | Sweet, like fresh bread | Bright and shiny
exercise: «Their fusty ideas about school were fifty years out of date.» What does fusty suggest about the ideas? | Exciting and new | Wet and muddy | *Old-fashioned and dull | Very kind
exercise: Find and copy the word that describes a smell that is stale and damp: «The cellar was cold, dark and fusty.» | dark | *fusty | cold | cellar
test: «Open the window, it's fusty in here!» What does fusty mean? | *Smelling stale and shut-in | Very cold to touch | Smelling of fresh flowers | Full of bright light
test: «Their fusty ideas about phones were out of date.» What kind of ideas does fusty describe here? | Very wet | *Old-fashioned and dull | Loud and funny | Fresh and modern
exam: «Mole came back to his shut-up home and found it fusty.» What does fusty mean? | *Smelling stale, damp and old | Full of loud music | Bright and cheerful | Very tall and thin
